course: dictionary
lesson: 1236
title: Bumblebees and their small nests
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A bumblebee is a large, round, hairy bee, often black and yellow. You do not need to know every word in a science text, because the words around a new word give clues. «On a cold spring morning a fat furry bumblebee queen is often the first bee out.» Fat, furry and first out tell you what a bumblebee looks like and when it appears.
explain: Look at «Bumblebee colonies are small, often a few dozen to a few hundred bees.» The word colonies is new. The clue is the numbers that follow: a few dozen to a few hundred bees. So a colony must be a group of bees that live together.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Bumblebee groups are small, often a few dozen to a few hundred bees» still makes sense, so your meaning fits. If it did not fit, you would try another meaning.
fact: A bumblebee is a large, round, hairy bee, often black and yellow, that buzzes loudly.
fact: Bumblebees collect nectar and pollen from flowers, and they are important pollinators that help plants make fruit and seeds.
fact: Bumblebees warm up by shivering their flight muscles, so they can fly on cold spring mornings.
fact: Bumblebee colonies are small, and only the new queens survive the winter, sleeping underground.
fact: Bumblebees are gentle and rarely sting unless squashed or bothered; anyone allergic must tell an adult.
exercise: «Bumblebees warm up by shivering their flight muscles, so they can fly on cold spring mornings when honeybees cannot.» What helps a bumblebee fly on a cold morning? | Its bright yellow colour | Sleeping under the ground all day | *Shivering its flight muscles to warm up | Eating a whole flower
exercise: «On a cold spring morning a fat furry bumblebee queen is often the first bee out.» Find and copy one word that describes the bee's coat. | morning | fat | *furry | cold
exercise: «Bumblebee colonies are small, often a few dozen to a few hundred bees.» How many bees might one bumblebee colony have? | Millions of bees | Exactly one hundred bees every time | *A few dozen to a few hundred bees | Just two bees
test: «Wasps and bumblebees do not usually die when they sting and can sting more than once.» What can a bumblebee do with its sting? | It stings only in winter | It loses its sting and dies after one sting | *It can sting more than once | It never stings anyone
test: «The horse chestnut's sticky buds burst open, and a huge furry queen bumblebee zigzags low over the lawn hunting for an old mouse hole to start her nest.» What is the queen bumblebee hunting for? | Frogspawn in the pond | A new hive made of wax | *An old mouse hole to start her nest | Flowers to drink from
exam: «In spring each queen starts a new nest alone.» What does alone mean here? | Under the frogspawn in the pond | *By herself, with no other bees | Together with her sisters | In a big hive full of bees
